5:[["$","$L10","2.12",{"topic":{"id":"2.12","title":"Challenges in Handling Electronic Evidence","minutes":13,"summary":"Plan for encryption, scale, cloud dependence, cross-border control, and fragile records without sacrificing rights or accuracy.","sections":[{"title":"Technical barriers","body":["Encryption can protect legitimate privacy while limiting access to evidence. The correct response is not to assume guilt from refusal or to try arbitrary passwords. Identify the encryption layer, device state, available backups, key custodians, and lawful options. A cloud export or previously unlocked session may be more proportionate than invasive access, but only where authorized and reliable.","Volume and variety create triage problems. Multiple devices can contain duplicates, synchronized records, and inconsistent clocks. Anti-forensic techniques may alter logs or timestamps. Use known-good references, independent corroboration, and explicit uncertainty. SSD behavior, proprietary apps, and unsupported formats can make a familiar tool’s output incomplete."]},{"title":"Organizational and cross-border barriers","body":["Cloud records may be controlled by a provider in another jurisdiction, stored across regions, and retained for a short period. A customer may possess only a limited audit-log export. Identify the tenant, account, service, region, custodian, and contractual access route. Send precise preservation and production requests through the competent channel, and record the provider’s response and limitations.","Human factors include incomplete complaints, pressure for quick attribution, lack of trained staff, and poor handoffs. Separate duties for collection, examination, and review where practical. Protect complainants and unrelated users by limiting access and redacting disclosure copies. Do not treat a victim’s private life as an unlimited investigative resource."]},{"title":"Defensible decisions under uncertainty","body":["Use a decision register for material trade-offs: risk, options, authority, chosen action, expected impact, and outcome. If evidence cannot be preserved perfectly, explain what was possible and why. A live capture may be the only practical route; a missing provider log may be irrecoverable. Honest limitations are part of the evidential record.","Quality assurance should include validated tools, documented methods, peer review, secure storage, and retention schedules. A laboratory cannot promise that every challenge has a technical solution. Its professional obligation is to use a suitable process, avoid overstatement, and make the resulting evidence understandable and open to appropriate scrutiny."]}],"practice":{"title":"The expiring cloud log","scenario":"A relevant audit log will expire soon, but the provider is overseas and the tenant administrator is unavailable.","steps":["Identify the custodian and urgent preservation options.","Record the retention deadline and source time zone.","Choose the competent request route and minimize the requested scope.","Document unavailable data and avoid claiming a complete reconstruction."],"debrief":"Early, precise preservation can matter more than a later perfect acquisition plan. Authority and honesty remain necessary when time is short."},"terms":[],"lawIds":["bnss","bsa","dpdp"],"sources":["privacy","nist-guide","budapest","bnss"],"labId":"$undefined","unit":2,"objectives":["Explain technical barriers and apply it to an investigation.","Explain organizational and cross-border barriers and apply it to an investigation.","Explain defensible decisions under uncertainty and apply it to an investigation."],"question":{"id":"q-2.12","prompt":"What is the most defensible response to an unavailable cloud record?","options":["Invent a plausible timestamp.","State the limitation, preserve related sources, and use lawful alternatives.","Assume the missing record proves the allegation.","Access an unrelated account without authority."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Missing data must be disclosed. Related records and lawful preservation may help, but they do not justify unsupported conclusions.","unit":2}}}]]
